{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/816770-homebrew-tzimisce-bloodline","id":816770,"title":"Homebrew: Tzimisce Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-26T04:29:05-08:00","id":816770,"title":"Homebrew: Tzimisce Bloodline","content":"I've always been intrigued by the Tzimisce from Masquerade. So here is my attempt at converting them to requiem.I'm well aware that there have been many, many such conversion proposed before. With vicissitude modeled as anything from discipline to devotions to blood sorcery and even supernatural merits. No approach ever truly satisfied me, either being too limited or too complex with long, long list or tables of potential options. <br /> <br /> So here is my own novel approach. Vicissitude as a slightly modified influence.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lu23cJtnkKKFKQ-ocr2BHQJxTCoecAaUbJnIzH9G8sk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Tzimisces</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T04:46:58-08:00","id":816777,"title":"","content":"Immediately I dislike the bloodlines gift dependency on Dominate. What if I don't want to have Dominate and still be part of Tzimisce? Especially because Gangrel is a clan for this, so it should be possible to be a Tzimisce with no Dominate at all. <br /> <br /> I also have a slight dislike towards &quot;capped by humanity&quot;, I much prefer to apply the human interaction penalty (which depends on Humanity) towards associated actions.<br /> <br /> Other than that... I'm not sure on the merge between Discipline and Devotion to create the influence like thing, but it's more or less fine. <br /> <br /> Of course this needs more thought in terms of actual capabilities. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T15:08:05-08:00","id":817196,"title":"","content":"Actually I like that it requires dominate, as the ability isn't just used on you. But I think there should be more to the gift than just the... odd discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}